  biomeName: Silt Catacombs
  minDepthMeters: 3000
  maxDepthMeters: 3500
  shortDescription: Roofless tunnels left by extinct mega-worms.
  isPlaceholder: 0
  visitPurpose: Transition biome. Come here to push deeper, find better materials,
    and follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  commonRewardHook: Reliable value comes from Abyssal Crystal and Rare Earth Dust.
  rareRewardHook: 'The rare pull is real: Gold Ore and Abyss Pressure Shell.'
  landmarkIdentity: Silt Catacombs reads through spires, steps, and big natural crowns.
    Landmarks should feel large and route-defining.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets exist, but they must be earned by reading the
    terrain.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines, then overstaying
    for loot. Creature pressure stays extreme.'
  extractionFocus: 'Minimal contact count, extreme commitment, almost no comfort.
    Mid-depth: favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes, then return before greed
    stretches the route.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is the final shaft or void cut. This slot should
    read through void-rim terraces and black pressure cuts; use vertical forms to
    keep heading.
